# Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)

Lighthouse accessibility >= 95 is enforced in `lighthouserc.cjs`; the rest requires manual checks. Accessibility is also an SEO and AdSense (UX) signal.

## Forms and calculators
- Every input has a visible `<label>` (wrapping `<label class="field">` is the house pattern), unit text, and an optional `.hint`. Placeholder text is never the label.
- Correct types: `type="number"` + `inputmode="decimal"`, `min`/`max`/`step`; `<select>` for enumerations; radio groups in `<fieldset><legend>`.
- No input-time validation errors that steal focus. Invalid input hides results (`showResults(panel, false)`) and, where helpful, shows a text message in an `aria-live="polite"` region.
- Results panel: `aria-live="polite"`, updated as text; do not rely on colour, charts or canvas alone: provide a text summary and table alternative.
- Unit toggles are real `<button type="button" aria-pressed>` elements (see `wireWeightUnitToggle` in `calc-utils.ts`), keyboard operable, with visible labels ("lb", "kg").
- Calculators are fully usable with keyboard only and with 200% text zoom / 320 px width (reflow), no horizontal scroll, no hover-only controls.

## Structure and content
- One `<h1>`; logical heading order; landmarks (`<header>`, `<nav aria-label>`, `<main id="main-content">`, `<footer>`); the skip link in `BaseLayout.astro` stays first in the tab order.
- Link text describes the destination (no "click here"); links that open a new tab say so and use `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Tables: `<th scope>`, captions or a preceding heading; responsive wrappers use `overflow-x: auto` with `tabindex="0"` and an accessible name.
- Images: meaningful `alt` or `alt=""` if decorative; SVG decorations `aria-hidden="true"`; charts have a text alternative.
- `<html lang="en">`; avoid auto-playing or moving content; no pop-ups/interstitials; the cookie notice is a dialog with a focusable "Accept" button and does not trap focus.
- Do not use `title` for essential info; do not remove focus outlines.

## Visual
- Text contrast >= 4.5:1 (large text and UI components >= 3:1). Check any colour you add to `src/styles/global.css` against its background, including warning/disclaimer boxes and the ad placeholder.
- Visible `:focus-visible` style on all interactive elements.
- Tap targets >= 24x24 CSS px (WCAG 2.2 target size minimum); prefer 44 px for primary buttons.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; no essential information conveyed by colour alone.
- Ads: label "Advertisement"; `AdSlot` has an `aria-label`; never place ads between a form field and its result.

## Test before merging UI changes
1. Keyboard-only pass through the page (Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter/Space on buttons/selects).
2. Screen-reader spot check (VoiceOver or NVDA): labels read, result announced on change, headings navigable.
3. 320 px width and 200% zoom, no clipped content.
4. `npm run lhci` accessibility >= 95 for the changed template (axe-based audits `color-contrast`, `image-alt`, `link-text` are errors).
5. Emulate `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` and forced-colors if you changed styling.
